Create, inspect, update, and delete Moment posts.

Usage:
  moment post [flags]
  moment post [command]

Available Commands:
  create      Publish a Moment post
  delete      Delete a Moment post
  get         Get one Moment post
  list        List the public Moment timeline
  update      Update a Moment post

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for post

Global Flags:
      --data-dir string     local Moment data directory (direct mode)
      --json                write one machine-readable JSON document to stdout
      --log-format string   stderr log format: text or json (default "text")
      --log-level string    stderr log level: error, warn, info, or debug (default "info")
      --no-input            fail instead of prompting for input
      --timeout duration    maximum command duration (default 30s)
      --token-file string   file containing the owner API token
      --url string          Moment HTTP API base URL (API mode)

Use "moment post [command] --help" for more information about a command.
